"q-auction-basics-0":{"target":{"node":"auctions","href":"../math/applied/auction-basics/#step2"},"prompts":[{"node":"auctions","ask":{"zh":"第一价格拍卖里，为什么中标者总想压一点价？第二价格里，说出真实估值会亏吗？","en":"In a first-price auction, why does the winner always want to shade the bid a little? In a second-price auction, can telling your true value lose you money?"}},{"node":"game-theory","ask":{"zh":"“占优策略”是什么意思？为什么第二价格里的真话策略不用猜对手出什么？","en":"What does a “dominant strategy” mean? Why does truth-telling in second-price need no guess about rivals?"}}],"reveal":{"zh":"第二价格拍卖里，说真话是占优策略：出价只决定你是否中标，不决定你付多少钱，付的是第二高价；第一价格里中标即按自己出价付款，所以人人压价。英式等价于第二价格、荷式等价于第一价格，平均收益相等；真值不确定时还要小心赢家的诅咒。","en":"In a second-price auction truth-telling is dominant: your bid only decides whether you win, not what you pay — you pay the second-highest bid. In a first-price auction you pay your own bid when you win, so everyone shades; English matches second-price and Dutch matches first-price with equal average revenue, and with uncertain true values, beware the winner's curse."},"source":"../math/applied/auction-basics/#step2","lesson":"auction-basics"},
"q-fees-compounding-0":{"target":{"node":"fees-compounding","href":"../investment/rates/fees-compounding/#step4"},"prompts":[{"node":"compound-interest","ask":{"zh":"10000 按 5% 复利 30 年是多少？按 4% 呢？","en":"What do 10,000 grow to over 30 years at 5%, and at 4%?"}},{"node":"fees-compounding","ask":{"zh":"两个结果差多少？占不收费终值的几成？","en":"How far apart are the two, as a share of the no-fee result?"}}],"reveal":{"zh":"1% 的年费相当于把 5% 的年收益降成 4%：30 年后 10000 分别变成约 43200 和约 32400，差约 10800，大约是不收费终值的四分之一。","en":"A 1% annual fee turns a 5% return into 4%: after 30 years 10,000 becomes about 43,200 versus about 32,400 — a gap of about 10,800, roughly a quarter of the no-fee result."},"source":"../investment/rates/fees-compounding/#step4","lesson":"fees-compounding"},
"q-interest-rates-bonds-0":{"target":{"node":"interest-rates-bonds","href":"../investment/rates/interest-rates-bonds/#step3"},"prompts":[{"node":"compound-interest","ask":{"zh":"5 年后的 1000，利率 5% 和 8% 时今天各值多少？","en":"What is 1,000 due in 5 years worth today at 5% and at 8%?"}},{"node":"interest-rates-bonds","ask":{"zh":"新债券付 8%，只付 5% 的旧债券还能按 1000 卖出去吗？","en":"If new bonds pay 8%, can an old 5% bond still sell for 1,000?"}}],"reveal":{"zh":"债券价格是未来现金按当前利率折现的总和。利率升到 8%，同样的未来现金今天更不值钱；而且新债券付 8%，旧债只付 5%，只有降价到买家也能拿到 8% 才卖得掉。","en":"A bond’s price is its future cash discounted at the current rate. When rates rise to 8%, the same future payments are worth less today; and with new bonds paying 8% against the old one’s 5%, the old bond sells only once its price falls far enough for the buyer to earn 8% as well."},"source":"../investment/rates/interest-rates-bonds/#step3","lesson":"interest-rates-bonds"}
